== Recent News

- \[July 2024\] We released the full [https://github.com/NVlabs/mimicgen MimicGen data generation code]! Easily generate large-scale robot demonstrations from just a few human demonstrations.

- \[July 2024\] We are organizing the [https://sites.google.com/view/data-generation-for-robotics/home?authuser=0 Data Generation for Robotics] workshop at RSS 2024!

- \[July 2024\] [https://robocasa.ai/ RoboCasa] presented at RSS 2024. It is a large-scale simulation framework for training robots to complete everyday tasks, with a focus on leveraging generative AI tools. Checkout the [https://github.com/robocasa/robocasa code and datasets] generated by [https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen].

- \[July 2024\] [https://sites.google.com/view/intervengen2024 IntervenGen] was accepted at IROS 2024! It is our new data generation system that extends [https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen] to the interactive imitation learning setting.

== About Me

I am a research scientist at NVIDIA AI. I obtained my PhD degree from Stanford University, co-advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. My research focuses on developing systems and algorithms to enable robots to learn useful manipulation tasks.

